 about the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase/repos/beads` sidecar root so design/plan reference resolution [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]keeps working once bead state leaves the plans repo.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Beads sidecar README and infographic[/bold #D7AFFF]                          [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]guide[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]guide: author the generated beads sidecar README template plus its [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]GPT-image 1600x900 directory-map infographic and prompt record, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]split the guide-kind constant from the legacy directory-README constant.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Schema v3 store record and beads kind resolution[/bold #D7AFFF]              [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]record[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]record: add an optional `beads` sidecar to the SDD store record at [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]schema version 3, resolve `kind_root(\"beads\")` and a per-kind repo root [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]from it, and keep schema-2 records resolving bead state to the plans [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sidecar unchanged.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  4 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Beads sidecar registration and inventory[/bold #D7AFFF]                      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]config[dim] · [dim][/dim]after record[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]config: register `beads` as a managed sidecar role across defaults, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]identity, clone-dir mapping, repo inventory, `sase repo path`, doctor [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]storage checks, and the config schema, gating auto-clone on a recorded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]beads sidecar.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  5 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Repo-root bead store layout[/bold #D7AFFF]                                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]rootstore[dim] · [dim][/dim]after core, record[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]rootstore: support a bead store whose files live at the repository root,[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]covering the beads dirname constant, gitignore patterns, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]conflict-resolver prefix handling, bead location resolution, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]project-root and bead-directory heuristics.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  6 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Commit, push, lock, and attribution routing[/bold #D7AFFF]                   [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]commit[dim] · [dim][/dim]after record, rootstore[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]commit: route bead commits, pushes, locks, health checks, agent env [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]vars, and commit attribution to the beads repository instead of the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]plans repository.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  7 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Lazy beads sidecar materialization[/bold #D7AFFF]                            [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]lazyclone[dim] · [dim][/dim]after config, rootstore[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]lazyclone: make `sase bead` clone the beads sidecar on demand when [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`sase/repos/beads` is missing, mirroring how `sase repo open` and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`--ensure` materialize sidecars.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  8 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Beads sidecar initialization and adoption transaction[/bold #D7AFFF]         [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]init[dim] · [dim][/dim]after guide, config, rootstore, commit[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]init: create, seed, and record the beads sidecar from `sase repo init`, [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]including the rerunnable record-last transaction that adopts existing [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bead state out of the plans sidecar.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  9 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Documentation refresh[/bold #D7AFFF]                                         [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]docs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after init[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]docs: update SDD storage, beads, and init documentation plus the plans [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]sidecar README for the new beads repository, its layout, and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]adoption flow.[/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  10 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Migrate the enabled projects[/bold #D7AFFF]                                 [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]migrate[dim] · [dim][/dim]after init, commit, lazyclone, docs[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]migrate: run and verify the adoption against the sase, actstat, and [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]bob-cli projects, then confirm bead reads, writes, and workspace clones [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]against the new sidecar.[/#D7D7AF]","clan_tribe":"epic","epic_bead_id":"sase-a8","llm_provider":"codex","model":"gpt-5.5","phase_bead_id":"sase-a8.1","reasoning_effort":"xhigh","vcs_provider":"GitHub"},"source_run_id":"run-1da86682fe9f9be0e0f406c21efd156e","started_at":"2026-07-27T19:58:03.247890+00:00","state":"completed"},{"commits":[{"committed_at":1785185022,"sha":"c113156466bd746064212cfe48e80fc74073ffe3","subject":"feat: register beads as a managed sidecar (sase-a8.4)"}],"dismissed_at":null,"files":{"chat":{"digest":"95df8d1ec02f9473f284c703248034eb9857ad13d9cd4a63c507f91f5432157d","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a8.4/chat.md","size_bytes":5137},"commits":{"digest":"bfe91d0662a67449f28af9baf9d1b86528b94914650efc4f93cb00a33ca73923","path":"agents/bbugyi200.athena.sase-a8.4/commits.json","size_bytes":231},"embedded_workflows":{"digest":"a398c70160fe308637edd70b38d8cf02cc697183c480675d10f387d529663058","path":"agents/bbug